# Scaffold Hire

Track hired scaffolding, its rate and its off-hire date.

This module was generated from a specification rather than written by hand.
`spec.json` beside this file is that specification, and it is also what the
platform renders the screen from.

## Record: Hire

| Field | Label | Type | Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| `reference` | Reference | text | yes |
| `notes` | Notes | long_text | no |
| `bay_count` | Bays | integer | yes |
| `area_m2` | Area | number | no |
| `weekly_rate` | Weekly rate | money | yes |
| `on_hire_date` | On hire | date | yes |
| `off_hire_date` | Off hire | date | no |
| `inspected_at` | Last inspection | datetime | no |
| `is_tagged` | Tagged | boolean | no |
| `status` | Status | select | yes |

## Rules

- `REFERENCE_REQUIRED` (error): A hire needs a reference to be found by.
- `RATE_POSITIVE` (error): A weekly rate must be above zero.
- `BAYS_IN_RANGE` (error): A hire covers between 1 and 500 bays.
- `STATUS_KNOWN` (error): Status must be one the register recognises.
- `INSPECTION_NOT_FUTURE` (error): An inspection cannot be recorded before it happens.
- `OFF_HIRE_AFTER_ON_HIRE` (error): Off hire cannot precede on hire.

## API

Mounted at `/api/v1/scaffold-hire`.

- `GET /ui-spec` the screen description
- `GET /` list, `GET /{id}` one
- `POST /` create, `PATCH /{id}` update, `DELETE /{id}` remove

Reading needs `scaffold_hire.read`, writing needs `scaffold_hire.write`.
